```

Supplier is executed only when value is absent.

---

# Supplier vs Function

| Supplier | Function |
|-----------|-----------|
| No Input | Input Required |
| Returns Output | Returns Output |
| get() | apply() |

Supplier:

```java
Supplier<String> s =
        () -> "Java";
```

Function:

```java
Function<String,Integer> f =
        str -> str.length();
```

---

# Supplier vs Consumer

| Supplier | Consumer |
|-----------|-----------|
| No Input | Input Required |
| Returns Output | No Output |
| get() | accept() |

Supplier:

```java
Supplier<String> s =
        () -> "Java";
```

Consumer:

```java
Consumer<String> c =
        str -> System.out.println(str);
```

---

# Supplier vs Predicate

| Supplier | Predicate |
|-----------|-----------|
| No Input | Input Required |
| Returns Value | Returns Boolean |
| get() | test() |

Supplier:

```java
Supplier<String> s =
        () -> "Java";
```

Predicate:

```java
Predicate<Integer> p =
        n -> n % 2 == 0;
```

