### 🔷 Category 3 (continued): Spring Boot — Testing

| # | Annotation | Framework / Module | Core Purpose & When to Use | Code Example |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 61 | `@SpringBootTest` | Spring Boot Test | Loads the **full application context** for integration tests. Use `webEnvironment = RANDOM_PORT` to spin up a real server. Slower than slice tests — reserve for true end-to-end integration scenarios. | `@SpringBootTest(`<br>`  webEnvironment = SpringBootTest.WebEnvironment.RANDOM_PORT)`<br>`@ActiveProfiles("test")`<br>`class OrderApiIntegrationTest {`<br>`  @Autowired private TestRestTemplate restTemplate;`<br>`  @Test`<br>`  void shouldCreateOrder() {`<br>`    ResponseEntity<Order> res = restTemplate.postForEntity("/api/orders", request, Order.class);`<br>`    assertThat(res.getStatusCode()).isEqualTo(HttpStatus.CREATED);`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 62 | `@WebMvcTest` | Spring Boot Test | Loads **only the web layer** (Controllers, Filters, `@ControllerAdvice`) — no Service or Repository beans. Fast. Use `@MockBean` for service-layer dependencies. Best for testing request validation, response serialization, and error handling. | `@WebMvcTest(UserController.class)`<br>`class UserControllerTest {`<br>`  @Autowired private MockMvc mockMvc;`<br>`  @MockBean private UserService userService;`<br>`  @Test`<br>`  void shouldReturn400WhenEmailInvalid() throws Exception {`<br>`    mockMvc.perform(post("/users").contentType(APPLICATION_JSON)`<br>`      .content("{\"email\":\"bad\"}")).andExpect(status().isBadRequest());`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 63 | `@DataJpaTest` | Spring Boot Test | Loads **only JPA components** (entities, repositories) with an in-memory H2 database (by default). Auto-rolls back each test. Perfect for testing custom `@Query` methods and entity mappings without the full context. | `@DataJpaTest`<br>`class EmployeeRepositoryTest {`<br>`  @Autowired private EmployeeRepository repo;`<br>`  @Test`<br>`  void shouldFindByEmail() {`<br>`    repo.save(new Employee("john@tcs.com", "John"));`<br>`    Optional<Employee> found = repo.findByEmail("john@tcs.com");`<br>`    assertThat(found).isPresent();`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 64 | `@MockBean` | Spring Boot Test | Adds a **Mockito mock** to the Spring `ApplicationContext`, replacing any existing bean of the same type. Used in `@SpringBootTest` and `@WebMvcTest` to stub collaborators without loading their full implementation. | `@WebMvcTest(PaymentController.class)`<br>`class PaymentControllerTest {`<br>`  @Autowired private MockMvc mockMvc;`<br>`  @MockBean private PaymentService paymentService;`<br>`  @Test`<br>`  void shouldProcessPayment() throws Exception {`<br>`    given(paymentService.charge(any())).willReturn(new Receipt("TXN001"));`<br>`    mockMvc.perform(post("/payments")...)`<br>`      .andExpect(jsonPath("$.txnId").value("TXN001"));`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 65 | `@TestConfiguration` | Spring Boot Test | Defines beans **exclusively for test contexts** without affecting production beans. Use to provide test doubles, custom test data factories, or override `@Primary` beans only during tests. | `@TestConfiguration`<br>`public class TestMailConfig {`<br>`  @Bean`<br>`  @Primary`<br>`  public JavaMailSender fakeMailSender() {`<br>`    return new FakeJavaMailSender(); // no real emails sent in tests`<br>`  }`<br>`}`<br><br>`@SpringBootTest`<br>`@Import(TestMailConfig.class)`<br>`class NotificationServiceTest { ... }` |

