### 🔷 Category 4: Spring Web / REST

| # | Annotation | Framework / Module | Core Purpose & When to Use | Code Example |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 66 | `@RestController` | Spring Web MVC | Composite of `@Controller` + `@ResponseBody`. Every method return value is serialized directly to the HTTP response body (JSON by default via Jackson). The standard annotation for all REST API controllers. | `@RestController`<br>`@RequestMapping("/api/v1/products")`<br>`@RequiredArgsConstructor`<br>`public class ProductController {`<br>`  private final ProductService productService;`<br>`  @GetMapping("/{id}")`<br>`  public ResponseEntity<ProductDto> getById(@PathVariable Long id) {`<br>`    return ResponseEntity.ok(productService.findById(id));`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 67 | `@RequestMapping` | Spring Web MVC | Maps HTTP requests to handler methods. Applied at **class level** to set the base path and at **method level** for specifics. Prefer `@GetMapping`, `@PostMapping`, etc. at method level — they''re more readable and less error-prone. | `@RestController`<br>`@RequestMapping(`<br>`  value = "/api/v2/orders",`<br>`  produces = MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON_VALUE)`<br>`public class OrderController {`<br>`  @RequestMapping(method = RequestMethod.GET, params = "status=PENDING")`<br>`  public List<Order> getPendingOrders() { ... }`<br>`}` |
| 68 | `@GetMapping` | Spring Web MVC | Shorthand for `@RequestMapping(method = GET)`. Use for **read operations** — fetching resources. Supports `path`, `params`, `headers`, `produces`. Always idempotent and safe — no side effects expected. | `@GetMapping(value = "/users", produces = APPLICATION_JSON_VALUE)`<br>`public ResponseEntity<Page<UserDto>> getAllUsers(`<br>`  @RequestParam(defaultValue = "0") int page,`<br>`  @RequestParam(defaultValue = "20") int size) {`<br>`  return ResponseEntity.ok(userService.findAll(PageRequest.of(page, size)));`<br>`}` |
| 69 | `@PostMapping` | Spring Web MVC | Shorthand for `@RequestMapping(method = POST)`. Use for **resource creation**. Return `201 Created` with `Location` header as REST best practice. Not idempotent — calling twice creates two resources. | `@PostMapping`<br>`public ResponseEntity<OrderDto> createOrder(`<br>`  @Valid @RequestBody CreateOrderRequest request,`<br>`  UriComponentsBuilder ucb) {`<br>`  OrderDto created = orderService.create(request);`<br>`  URI location = ucb.path("/api/orders/{id}").buildAndExpand(created.getId()).toUri();`<br>`  return ResponseEntity.created(location).body(created);`<br>`}` |
| 70 | `@PutMapping` | Spring Web MVC | Shorthand for `@RequestMapping(method = PUT)`. Use for **full resource replacement**. Must be idempotent — calling N times yields same result. Requires the entire resource representation in the body. | `@PutMapping("/{id}")`<br>`public ResponseEntity<EmployeeDto> updateEmployee(`<br>`  @PathVariable Long id,`<br>`  @Valid @RequestBody UpdateEmployeeRequest request) {`<br>`  return ResponseEntity.ok(employeeService.update(id, request));`<br>`}` |
| 71 | `@DeleteMapping` | Spring Web MVC | Shorthand for `@RequestMapping(method = DELETE)`. Use for **resource deletion**. Idempotent. Return `204 No Content` on success (no body). Return `404` if resource not found. | `@DeleteMapping("/{id}")`<br>`@ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.NO_CONTENT)`<br>`public void deleteUser(@PathVariable Long id) {`<br>`  userService.deleteById(id);`<br>`  // 204 returned automatically via @ResponseStatus`<br>`}` |
| 72 | `@PatchMapping` | Spring Web MVC | Shorthand for `@RequestMapping(method = PATCH)`. Use for **partial resource updates** — only send changed fields. Not necessarily idempotent. Combine with `@RequestBody Map<String, Object>` or a dedicated patch DTO. | `@PatchMapping("/{id}/status")`<br>`public ResponseEntity<OrderDto> updateStatus(`<br>`  @PathVariable Long id,`<br>`  @RequestBody Map<String, String> patch) {`<br>`  String newStatus = patch.get("status");`<br>`  return ResponseEntity.ok(orderService.updateStatus(id, newStatus));`<br>`}` |
| 73 | `@RequestBody` | Spring Web MVC | Deserializes the **HTTP request body** into a Java object (via `HttpMessageConverter`, usually Jackson). Works with `@Valid` for bean validation. Required for `POST`/`PUT`/`PATCH` endpoints receiving JSON payloads. | `@PostMapping("/login")`<br>`public ResponseEntity<AuthResponse> login(`<br>`  @RequestBody @Valid LoginRequest loginRequest) {`<br>`  String token = authService.authenticate(`<br>`    loginRequest.getUsername(), loginRequest.getPassword());`<br>`  return ResponseEntity.ok(new AuthResponse(token));`<br>`}` |
| 74 | `@PathVariable` | Spring Web MVC | Binds a **URI template variable** (e.g., `{id}`) to a method parameter. Variable name must match the template placeholder unless `name` attribute is specified. Supports type conversion — Spring auto-converts `String` to `Long`, `UUID`, etc. | `@GetMapping("/departments/{deptId}/employees/{empId}")`<br>`public ResponseEntity<EmployeeDto> getEmployee(`<br>`  @PathVariable("deptId") Long departmentId,`<br>`  @PathVariable Long empId) {`<br>`  return ResponseEntity.ok(`<br>`    employeeService.findByDeptAndId(departmentId, empId));`<br>`}` |
| 75 | `@RequestParam` | Spring Web MVC | Binds an **HTTP query parameter** (or form field) to a method parameter. Supports `required` (default `true`), `defaultValue`, and collections (`?ids=1&ids=2`). Use `@RequestParam Map<String, String>` to capture all params dynamically. | `@GetMapping("/search")`<br>`public ResponseEntity<List<ProductDto>> search(`<br>`  @RequestParam String keyword,`<br>`  @RequestParam(required = false, defaultValue = "price") String sortBy,`<br>`  @RequestParam(required = false) List<String> categories) {`<br>`  return ResponseEntity.ok(productService.search(keyword, sortBy, categories));`<br>`}` |
| 76 | `@RequestHeader` | Spring Web MVC | Binds an **HTTP request header** to a method parameter. Use for extracting `Authorization`, `X-Correlation-ID`, `X-Tenant-ID`, API version headers. Supports `required` and `defaultValue`. | `@GetMapping("/me")`<br>`public ResponseEntity<UserDto> getCurrentUser(`<br>`  @RequestHeader("Authorization") String authHeader,`<br>`  @RequestHeader(value = "X-Correlation-ID", required = false)`<br>`    String correlationId) {`<br>`  MDC.put("correlationId", correlationId);`<br>`  return ResponseEntity.ok(userService.fromToken(authHeader));`<br>`}` |
| 77 | `@ResponseStatus` | Spring Web MVC | Sets the **HTTP status code** (and optional reason phrase) returned by a handler method or exception class. Cleaner than returning `ResponseEntity` when the status is always fixed and no body customization is needed. | `@ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.ACCEPTED)`<br>`@PostMapping("/emails/send-async")`<br>`public void sendEmailAsync(@Valid @RequestBody EmailRequest request) {`<br>`  emailQueue.enqueue(request); // 202 Accepted automatically`<br>`}`<br><br>`@ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND)`<br>`public class ResourceNotFoundException extends RuntimeException { ... }` |
| 78 | `@ExceptionHandler` | Spring Web MVC | Handles **specific exceptions thrown** within a `@Controller` or globally in a `@ControllerAdvice`. Returns a custom error response. Method signature is flexible — can accept the exception, `HttpServletRequest`, `WebRequest`, etc. | `@RestControllerAdvice`<br>`public class GlobalExceptionHandler {`<br>`  @ExceptionHandler(ResourceNotFoundException.class)`<br>`  @ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND)`<br>`  public ErrorResponse handleNotFound(ResourceNotFoundException ex, WebRequest req) {`<br>`    return new ErrorResponse("NOT_FOUND", ex.getMessage(),`<br>`      ((ServletWebRequest)req).getRequest().getRequestURI());`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 79 | `@RestControllerAdvice` | Spring Web MVC | Composite of `@ControllerAdvice` + `@ResponseBody`. A **global exception handler** for all REST controllers. Centralizes error handling — every `@ExceptionHandler` inside it automatically serializes the return value to JSON. | `@RestControllerAdvice`<br>`@Slf4j`<br>`public class ApiExceptionHandler {`<br>`  @ExceptionHandler(MethodArgumentNotValidException.class)`<br>`  @ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST)`<br>`  public ErrorResponse handleValidation(MethodArgumentNotValidException ex) {`<br>`    List<String> errors = ex.getBindingResult().getFieldErrors()`<br>`      .stream().map(e -> e.getField() + ": " + e.getDefaultMessage()).toList();`<br>`    return new ErrorResponse("VALIDATION_FAILED", errors);`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 80 | `@CrossOrigin` | Spring Web MVC | Enables **CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing)** at controller or method level. Specify `origins`, `methods`, `allowedHeaders`, `maxAge`. For global CORS, prefer `WebMvcConfigurer.addCorsMappings()` instead of scattering this annotation. | `@CrossOrigin(`<br>`  origins = {"https://app.company.com", "https://admin.company.com"},`<br>`  methods = {RequestMethod.GET, RequestMethod.POST},`<br>`  allowedHeaders = {"Authorization", "Content-Type"},`<br>`  maxAge = 3600)`<br>`@RestController`<br>`public class PublicApiController { ... }` |
| 81 | `@CookieValue` | Spring Web MVC | Binds an **HTTP cookie value** to a method parameter. Use for session tokens, tracking IDs, or A/B test flags passed via cookies. Supports `required` and `defaultValue`. | `@GetMapping("/dashboard")`<br>`public ResponseEntity<DashboardData> getDashboard(`<br>`  @CookieValue(value = "SESSIONID", required = false)`<br>`    String sessionId,`<br>`  @CookieValue(value = "ab-variant", defaultValue = "A")`<br>`    String abVariant) {`<br>`  return ResponseEntity.ok(dashboardService.get(sessionId, abVariant));`<br>`}` |

