### 🔷 Category 5: Spring Data JPA & Transactions

| # | Annotation | Framework / Module | Core Purpose & When to Use | Code Example |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 82 | `@Transactional` | Spring TX (`org.springframework.transaction.annotation`) | Wraps a method or class in a DB transaction. Key attributes: `propagation` (REQUIRED, REQUIRES_NEW, NESTED), `isolation` (READ_COMMITTED default), `readOnly = true` (optimizes read-only queries), `rollbackFor`. **Always apply at Service layer**, never at Controller or Repository. | `@Service`<br>`public class TransferService {`<br>`  @Transactional(isolation = Isolation.READ_COMMITTED,`<br>`    rollbackFor = InsufficientFundsException.class)`<br>`  public void transfer(Long fromId, Long toId, BigDecimal amount) {`<br>`    accountRepo.debit(fromId, amount);`<br>`    accountRepo.credit(toId, amount); // atomic — both or neither`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 83 | `@Query` | Spring Data JPA | Defines a **JPQL or native SQL query** directly on a repository method. Use when derived query method names become unreadable. Add `nativeQuery = true` for DB-specific SQL (e.g., window functions, CTEs). | `@Repository`<br>`public interface OrderRepository extends JpaRepository<Order, Long> {`<br>`  @Query("SELECT o FROM Order o JOIN FETCH o.items`<br>`         WHERE o.customer.id = :custId AND o.status = :status")`<br>`  List<Order> findByCustomerAndStatus(`<br>`    @Param("custId") Long customerId,`<br>`    @Param("status") OrderStatus status);`<br>`}` |
| 84 | `@Modifying` | Spring Data JPA | Required on `@Query` methods that execute **DML (UPDATE/DELETE)**. Without it, Spring treats the query as a SELECT and throws an exception. Combine with `@Transactional` — DML requires an active transaction. | `@Modifying`<br>`@Transactional`<br>`@Query("UPDATE Employee e SET e.salary = e.salary * :multiplier`<br>`       WHERE e.department.id = :deptId")`<br>`int applyDeptSalaryHike(`<br>`  @Param("deptId") Long deptId,`<br>`  @Param("multiplier") BigDecimal multiplier);` |
| 85 | `@Param` | Spring Data JPA | Binds a method parameter to a named parameter in a `@Query` expression (`:paramName`). Required when Java''s `-parameters` compiler flag is absent. Always use it explicitly to avoid position-sensitive bugs. | `@Query("SELECT u FROM User u WHERE u.email = :email AND u.active = :active")`<br>`Optional<User> findActiveByEmail(`<br>`  @Param("email") String email,`<br>`  @Param("active") boolean active);` |
| 86 | `@Lock` | Spring Data JPA | Applies a **JPA `LockModeType`** to a repository query method. Use `PESSIMISTIC_WRITE` for "select for update" semantics in critical sections (inventory deduction, seat booking). Complements `@Version` for optimistic locking. | `@Lock(LockModeType.PESSIMISTIC_WRITE)`<br>`@Query("SELECT s FROM Stock s WHERE s.productId = :id")`<br>`Optional<Stock> findAndLockByProductId(@Param("id") Long id);`<br><br>// Usage in service:<br>`Stock stock = stockRepo.findAndLockByProductId(id)`<br>`  .orElseThrow();`<br>`stock.deduct(quantity); // safe from concurrent modification` |
| 87 | `@EntityGraph` | Spring Data JPA | Overrides the **default fetch plan** for a specific query — eager-loads specified associations without changing the entity''s `fetch = LAZY` default. Solves N+1 without writing JOIN FETCH in every `@Query`. | `@EntityGraph(attributePaths = {"items", "items.product", "customer"})`<br>`@Query("SELECT o FROM Order o WHERE o.id = :id")`<br>`Optional<Order> findByIdWithDetails(@Param("id") Long id);`<br><br>// Loads Order + Items + Product + Customer in ONE query |
| 88 | `@EnableJpaRepositories` | Spring Data JPA | Activates Spring Data JPA repository scanning. Auto-enabled in Spring Boot. Use manually in multi-datasource setups to point each `@EnableJpaRepositories` instance at a different `EntityManagerFactory` and `TransactionManager`. | `@Configuration`<br>`@EnableJpaRepositories(`<br>`  basePackages = "com.app.reporting.repository",`<br>`  entityManagerFactoryRef = "reportingEntityManagerFactory",`<br>`  transactionManagerRef = "reportingTransactionManager")`<br>`public class ReportingDataSourceConfig { ... }` |
| 89 | `@Cacheable` | Spring Cache (`org.springframework.cache.annotation`) | Marks a method whose **return value should be cached**. On first call, executes the method and caches the result. On subsequent calls with the same key, returns from cache without executing the method. Works with Redis, Caffeine, EhCache etc. | `@Service`<br>`public class ProductService {`<br>`  @Cacheable(value = "products", key = "#id",`<br>`    unless = "#result == null")`<br>`  public ProductDto findById(Long id) {`<br>`    return productRepository.findById(id)`<br>`      .map(productMapper::toDto)`<br>`      .orElse(null);`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 90 | `@CacheEvict` | Spring Cache | Removes one or all entries from a cache. Use on update/delete methods to keep cache consistent. `allEntries = true` nukes the entire cache — use carefully. Combine `@Cacheable` + `@CacheEvict` on a class with `@CacheConfig`. | `@CacheEvict(value = "products", key = "#id")`<br>`@Transactional`<br>`public ProductDto updateProduct(Long id, UpdateProductRequest req) {`<br>`  Product product = productRepository.findById(id).orElseThrow();`<br>`  productMapper.update(product, req);`<br>`  return productMapper.toDto(productRepository.save(product));`<br>`  // cache entry for this id is evicted after method returns`<br>`}` |
| 91 | `@CachePut` | Spring Cache | Always **executes the method AND updates the cache** — unlike `@Cacheable` which skips execution on a hit. Use on update operations to refresh the cache with the latest data in a single step. | `@CachePut(value = "employees", key = "#result.id")`<br>`@Transactional`<br>`public EmployeeDto updateEmployee(Long id, UpdateEmployeeRequest req) {`<br>`  Employee emp = employeeRepo.findById(id).orElseThrow();`<br>`  emp.setName(req.getName());`<br>`  emp.setSalary(req.getSalary());`<br>`  return employeeMapper.toDto(employeeRepo.save(emp));`<br>`  // cache refreshed with updated dto`<br>`}` |

---

### 🔷 Category 6: Spring Cloud & Microservices

| # | Annotation | Framework / Module | Core Purpose & When to Use | Code Example |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 92 | `@EnableDiscoveryClient` | Spring Cloud Netflix / Spring Cloud Commons | Activates **service registration and discovery** with Eureka, Consul, or Zookeeper. Auto-enabled if Spring Cloud and a discovery client are on the classpath. Add explicitly for clarity in microservice entry points. | `@SpringBootApplication`<br>`@EnableDiscoveryClient`<br>`public class InventoryServiceApp {`<br>`  public static void main(String[] args) {`<br>`    SpringApplication.run(InventoryServiceApp.class, args);`<br>`    // service registers as "inventory-service" in Eureka`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 93 | `@EnableEurekaServer` | Spring Cloud Netflix Eureka Server | Turns a Spring Boot app into a **Eureka Service Registry**. Used on your dedicated discovery-server module. All other microservices register with this server and query it for peer addresses. | `@SpringBootApplication`<br>`@EnableEurekaServer`<br>`public class EurekaServerApp {`<br>`  public static void main(String[] args) {`<br>`    SpringApplication.run(EurekaServerApp.class, args);`<br>`  }`<br>`}`<br>// application.yml: eureka.client.register-with-eureka: false |
| 94 | `@FeignClient` | Spring Cloud OpenFeign | Declares a **declarative HTTP client interface** backed by Eureka or a static URL. Spring generates a proxy at runtime. Use instead of `RestTemplate` / `WebClient` for inter-service calls — far less boilerplate. Pair with Resilience4j fallback. | `@FeignClient(`<br>`  name = "payment-service",`<br>`  fallbackFactory = PaymentClientFallbackFactory.class)`<br>`public interface PaymentClient {`<br>`  @PostMapping("/api/payments/charge")`<br>`  ResponseEntity<Receipt> charge(`<br>`    @RequestBody ChargeRequest request);`<br><br>`  @GetMapping("/api/payments/{txnId}")`<br>`  PaymentStatus getStatus(@PathVariable String txnId);`<br>`}` |
| 95 | `@EnableFeignClients` | Spring Cloud OpenFeign | Enables Feign client scanning. Required in the main app class or a configuration class. Specify `basePackages` in multi-module setups to avoid scanning the entire classpath. | `@SpringBootApplication`<br>`@EnableFeignClients(`<br>`  basePackages = "com.company.orderservice.client")`<br>`@EnableDiscoveryClient`<br>`public class OrderServiceApp {`<br>`  public static void main(String[] args) {`<br>`    SpringApplication.run(OrderServiceApp.class, args);`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 96 | `@LoadBalanced` | Spring Cloud LoadBalancer | Enables **client-side load balancing** on a `RestTemplate` or `WebClient.Builder` bean. The bean intercepts requests using logical service names (e.g., `http://user-service/api/users`) and resolves them via Eureka. | `@Configuration`<br>`public class RestTemplateConfig {`<br>`  @Bean`<br>`  @LoadBalanced`<br>`  public RestTemplate loadBalancedRestTemplate() {`<br>`    return new RestTemplate();`<br>`  }`<br>`}`<br>// Usage:<br>`restTemplate.getForObject(`<br>`  "http://inventory-service/api/stock/{id}", Stock.class, id);` |
| 97 | `@RefreshScope` | Spring Cloud Config | Makes a bean **re-instantiated** when a `/actuator/refresh` event is triggered (after config server update). Use on beans that read `@Value` or `@ConfigurationProperties` that must pick up live config changes without restart. | `@RestController`<br>`@RefreshScope`<br>`public class FeatureFlagController {`<br>`  @Value("${feature.new-checkout-flow:false}")`<br>`  private boolean newCheckoutEnabled;`<br><br>`  @GetMapping("/features/checkout")`<br>`  public boolean isNewCheckoutEnabled() {`<br>`    return newCheckoutEnabled; // updates live after /actuator/refresh`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 98 | `@CircuitBreaker` | Resilience4j Spring Boot (`io.github.resilience4j`) | Wraps a method with a **Circuit Breaker** — CLOSED (normal), OPEN (failing fast), HALF_OPEN (testing recovery). Specify `name` matching `application.yml` config and `fallbackMethod` signature matching the original method plus a `Throwable` param. | `@Service`<br>`public class OrderService {`<br>`  @CircuitBreaker(`<br>`    name = "paymentService",`<br>`    fallbackMethod = "paymentFallback")`<br>`  public Receipt chargeCustomer(ChargeRequest request) {`<br>`    return paymentClient.charge(request).getBody();`<br>`  }`<br>`  private Receipt paymentFallback(ChargeRequest req, Throwable t) {`<br>`    log.warn("Payment CB open: {}", t.getMessage());`<br>`    return Receipt.pending(req.getOrderId()); // graceful degradation`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 99 | `@Retry` | Resilience4j Spring Boot | Retries a method on failure up to a configured number of attempts with optional backoff. Apply to transient failures (network blips, DB connection drops). Configure `maxAttempts`, `waitDuration`, `retryExceptions` in `application.yml`. | `@Service`<br>`public class NotificationService {`<br>`  @Retry(name = "smsService", fallbackMethod = "smsFallback")`<br>`  public void sendSms(String mobile, String message) {`<br>`    smsGatewayClient.send(mobile, message); // retried up to 3 times`<br>`  }`<br>`  private void smsFallback(String mobile, String message, Exception e) {`<br>`    log.error("SMS failed after retries for {}. Queuing.", mobile);`<br>`    smsQueue.enqueue(new SmsTask(mobile, message));`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 100 | `@RateLimiter` | Resilience4j Spring Boot | Limits the **number of calls per time window** to a method. Throws `RequestNotPermitted` when the limit is exceeded. Use to protect downstream services from being overwhelmed during traffic spikes. Configure via `resilience4j.ratelimiter` in `application.yml`. | `@RestController`<br>`public class SearchController {`<br>`  @GetMapping("/search")`<br>`  @RateLimiter(`<br>`    name = "searchRateLimiter",`<br>`    fallbackMethod = "searchFallback")`<br>`  public List<ProductDto> search(@RequestParam String q) {`<br>`    return searchService.search(q);`<br>`  }`<br>`  private List<ProductDto> searchFallback(String q, RequestNotPermitted ex) {`<br>`    return cachedSearchService.getTopResults(); // serve stale cache`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |

