### 🔷 Category 10: Spring Cloud Gateway & Distributed Tracing

| # | Annotation | Framework / Module | Core Purpose & When to Use | Code Example |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 123 | `@NewSpan` | Micrometer Tracing / Spring Cloud Sleuth | Creates a **new distributed tracing span** around the annotated method. Span name defaults to the method name. Use for fine-grained tracing of critical business operations within a service, visible in Zipkin/Jaeger. | `@Service`<br>`public class CheckoutService {`<br>`  @NewSpan("checkout.process-payment")`<br>`  public Receipt processPayment(`<br>`    @SpanTag("order.id") Long orderId,`<br>`    PaymentRequest request) {`<br>`    return paymentGateway.charge(request);`<br>`    // span shows in Zipkin with tag order.id=<value>`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 124 | `@SpanTag` | Micrometer Tracing | Adds a **tag (key-value pair)** to the current or `@NewSpan`-created span. Tags appear in Zipkin/Jaeger and allow filtering traces. Apply to method parameters to automatically capture their values as span metadata. | `@Service`<br>`public class InventoryService {`<br>`  @NewSpan("inventory.reserve")`<br>`  public void reserve(`<br>`    @SpanTag("product.id") Long productId,`<br>`    @SpanTag("quantity") int qty,`<br>`    @SpanTag("warehouse.id") String warehouseId) {`<br>`    stockRepository.deduct(productId, qty, warehouseId);`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 125 | `@GatewayFilter` | Spring Cloud Gateway | Marks a class as a **Gateway Filter Factory** for request/response manipulation in Spring Cloud Gateway. Implement `GatewayFilter` and apply via route config in `application.yml`. Use for auth token forwarding, request/response logging, rate limiting at the gateway edge. | `@Component`<br>`public class JwtRelayGatewayFilterFactory`<br>`  extends AbstractGatewayFilterFactory<Object> {`<br>`  @Override`<br>`  public GatewayFilter apply(Object config) {`<br>`    return (exchange, chain) -> {`<br>`      String token = extractToken(exchange.getRequest());`<br>`      ServerHttpRequest mutatedReq = exchange.getRequest().mutate()`<br>`        .header("X-Internal-Token", token).build();`<br>`      return chain.filter(exchange.mutate().request(mutatedReq).build());`<br>`    };`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |

---

### 🔷 Category 11: OpenAPI 3 / Springdoc (Swagger)

| # | Annotation | Framework / Module | Core Purpose & When to Use | Code Example |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 126 | `@Tag` | Springdoc / OpenAPI 3 (`io.swagger.v3.oas.annotations`) | Groups API operations under a **named tag** in the Swagger UI. Apply at controller class level. The `name` appears as the section header in the UI, `description` provides context. | `@RestController`<br>`@RequestMapping("/api/v1/orders")`<br>`@Tag(`<br>`  name = "Order Management",`<br>`  description = "APIs for creating, tracking, and managing customer orders")`<br>`@RequiredArgsConstructor`<br>`public class OrderController {`<br>`  // all methods grouped under "Order Management" in Swagger UI`<br>`}` |
| 127 | `@Operation` | Springdoc / OpenAPI 3 | Documents an individual **API endpoint** — summary (short label), description (detailed explanation), `operationId` (unique ID for code generation), `tags`, and `deprecated`. Essential for auto-generating API client SDKs. | `@GetMapping("/{id}")`<br>`@Operation(`<br>`  summary = "Get order by ID",`<br>`  description = "Retrieves full order details including line items, status history,`<br>`                  and shipping info. Requires ROLE_USER or ROLE_ADMIN.",`<br>`  operationId = "getOrderById")`<br>`public ResponseEntity<OrderDto> getOrder(@PathVariable Long id) {`<br>`  return ResponseEntity.ok(orderService.findById(id));`<br>`}` |
| 128 | `@ApiResponse` | Springdoc / OpenAPI 3 | Documents a **specific HTTP response code** for an endpoint. Always document the unhappy paths too (400, 401, 403, 404, 500). Combine multiple via `@ApiResponses`. | `@PostMapping`<br>`@Operation(summary = "Create new order")`<br>`@ApiResponse(responseCode = "201", description = "Order created successfully")`<br>`@ApiResponse(responseCode = "400", description = "Invalid request body — validation failed")`<br>`@ApiResponse(responseCode = "409", description = "Duplicate order reference")`<br>`@ApiResponse(responseCode = "503", description = "Payment service unavailable")`<br>`public ResponseEntity<OrderDto> createOrder(`<br>`  @Valid @RequestBody CreateOrderRequest req) { ... }` |
| 129 | `@Parameter` | Springdoc / OpenAPI 3 | Documents an **individual API parameter** (path, query, header, cookie). Adds description, example, required flag, and schema constraints to the Swagger UI. Use on `@PathVariable`, `@RequestParam`, `@RequestHeader` method params. | `@GetMapping`<br>`public ResponseEntity<Page<OrderDto>> searchOrders(`<br>`  @Parameter(description = "Order status filter", example = "PENDING",`<br>`    schema = @Schema(allowableValues = {"PENDING","SHIPPED","DELIVERED"}))`<br>`  @RequestParam(required = false) String status,`<br>`  @Parameter(description = "Zero-based page number", example = "0")`<br>`  @RequestParam(defaultValue = "0") int page) { ... }` |
| 130 | `@Schema` | Springdoc / OpenAPI 3 | Describes the **structure of a model class or field** in the generated OpenAPI spec. Controls `description`, `example`, `allowableValues`, `format`, `minimum`, `maximum`, `pattern`. Applied on DTOs and their fields. | `@Schema(description = "Request body for creating a new order")`<br>`@Data`<br>`public class CreateOrderRequest {`<br>`  @Schema(description = "Customer ID", example = "1042", requiredMode = REQUIRED)`<br>`  @NotNull private Long customerId;`<br><br>`  @Schema(description = "Delivery address PIN code",`<br>`    example = "400614", pattern = "^[1-9][0-9]{5}$")`<br>`  @Pattern(regexp = "^[1-9][0-9]{5}$")`<br>`  private String pinCode;`<br>`}` |
| 131 | `@Hidden` | Springdoc / OpenAPI 3 | **Excludes** a controller, method, or model from the generated OpenAPI documentation. Use for internal endpoints, actuator endpoints, or admin APIs that should not be exposed in the public API spec. | `@RestController`<br>`@RequestMapping("/internal")`<br>`@Hidden // entire controller hidden from Swagger UI`<br>`public class InternalMaintenanceController {`<br>`  @GetMapping("/rebuild-index")`<br>`  public void rebuildSearchIndex() {`<br>`    searchService.rebuildIndex();`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 132 | `@OpenAPIDefinition` | Springdoc / OpenAPI 3 | Defines **global OpenAPI metadata** — API title, version, description, license, contact, and global security schemes. Place on the main application class or a dedicated config class. | `@OpenAPIDefinition(`<br>`  info = @Info(`<br>`    title = "Order Service API",`<br>`    version = "v2.1.0",`<br>`    description = "Core order management APIs for the e-commerce platform",`<br>`    contact = @Contact(name = "Platform Team", email = "platform@company.com")`<br>`  ),`<br>`  security = @SecurityRequirement(name = "bearerAuth")`<br>`)`<br>`@SpringBootApplication`<br>`public class OrderServiceApp { ... }` |
| 133 | `@SecurityRequirement` | Springdoc / OpenAPI 3 | Declares that an endpoint requires a **specific security scheme** (defined in `@OpenAPIDefinition`). Adds a padlock icon in Swagger UI and marks the endpoint as requiring authentication in the spec. | `@PostMapping("/checkout")`<br>`@Operation(summary = "Place order")`<br>`@SecurityRequirement(name = "bearerAuth")`<br>`public ResponseEntity<OrderDto> checkout(`<br>`  @Valid @RequestBody CheckoutRequest request,`<br>`  @AuthenticationPrincipal UserPrincipal user) {`<br>`  return ResponseEntity.status(201).body(`<br>`    orderService.checkout(request, user.getId()));`<br>`}` |

