### 🔷 Category 12: Actuator & Micrometer Observability

| # | Annotation | Framework / Module | Core Purpose & When to Use | Code Example |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 134 | `@Endpoint` | Spring Boot Actuator (`org.springframework.boot.actuate.endpoint.annotation`) | Creates a **custom Actuator endpoint** accessible via `/actuator/{id}`. Pair with `@ReadOperation`, `@WriteOperation`, `@DeleteOperation`. Use to expose internal diagnostics, config dumps, cache stats, or feature flag states. | `@Component`<br>`@Endpoint(id = "feature-flags")`<br>`public class FeatureFlagEndpoint {`<br>`  private final FeatureFlagService featureFlagService;`<br><br>`  @ReadOperation`<br>`  public Map<String, Boolean> getFlags() {`<br>`    return featureFlagService.getAllFlags();`<br>`  }`<br><br>`  @WriteOperation`<br>`  public void setFlag(@Selector String flagName, boolean enabled) {`<br>`    featureFlagService.setFlag(flagName, enabled);`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 135 | `@ReadOperation` | Spring Boot Actuator | Maps a method in an `@Endpoint` class to **HTTP GET** (or JMX read). The method is invoked when the actuator endpoint is queried. Return type is automatically serialized to JSON. | `@Component`<br>`@Endpoint(id = "circuit-breakers")`<br>`public class CircuitBreakerEndpoint {`<br>`  @Autowired private CircuitBreakerRegistry registry;`<br><br>`  @ReadOperation`<br>`  public List<Map<String, Object>> getCircuitBreakerStatus() {`<br>`    return registry.getAllCircuitBreakers().stream()`<br>`      .map(cb -> Map.of(`<br>`        "name", cb.getName(),`<br>`        "state", cb.getState().name(),`<br>`        "failureRate", cb.getMetrics().getFailureRate()))`<br>`      .toList();`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 136 | `@WriteOperation` | Spring Boot Actuator | Maps a method to **HTTP POST** on a custom `@Endpoint`. Use to trigger actions — cache eviction, config reload, thread dump initiation. Request body or path params are bound automatically from the operation parameters. | `@WriteOperation`<br>`public OperationResult evictCache(`<br>`  @Selector String cacheName) {`<br>`  cacheManager.getCache(cacheName).clear();`<br>`  return new OperationResult("EVICTED",`<br>`    "Cache ''" + cacheName + "'' cleared at " + Instant.now());`<br>`}` |
| 137 | `@Timed` | Micrometer (`io.micrometer.core.annotation`) | Automatically records **method execution time** as a Micrometer `Timer` metric. Requires `TimedAspect` bean. Metrics appear in Prometheus (`/actuator/prometheus`) as `method_timed_seconds`. Add `percentiles` for P95/P99 latency tracking. | `@Service`<br>`public class SearchService {`<br>`  @Timed(`<br>`    value = "search.execution.time",`<br>`    description = "Time taken to execute product search",`<br>`    percentiles = {0.5, 0.95, 0.99},`<br>`    extraTags = {"layer", "service"})`<br>`  public List<ProductDto> search(SearchRequest request) {`<br>`    return elasticsearchClient.search(request);`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 138 | `@Counted` | Micrometer | Records how many times a method is called as a Micrometer `Counter`. Requires `CountedAspect` bean. Use for tracking business events — order placements, failed logins, cache misses — separately from execution time. | `@Service`<br>`public class AuthService {`<br>`  @Counted(`<br>`    value = "auth.login.attempts",`<br>`    description = "Number of login attempts",`<br>`    extraTags = {"service", "auth"})`<br>`  public AuthResponse login(LoginRequest request) {`<br>`    return performAuthentication(request);`<br>`    // counter increments on every call`<br>`    // combine with @Timed for full observability`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 139 | `@Observed` | Micrometer Observation API (Spring Boot 3+) | **Single annotation** replacing both `@Timed` and `@Counted` — creates a full Micrometer `Observation` (metrics + distributed traces in one). The modern approach in Spring Boot 3+. Requires `ObservedAspect` bean. | `@Service`<br>`public class PaymentService {`<br>`  @Observed(`<br>`    name = "payment.charge",`<br>`    contextualName = "process-payment",`<br>`    lowCardinalityKeyValues = {"payment.type", "CARD"})`<br>`  public Receipt charge(ChargeRequest request) {`<br>`    return paymentGateway.process(request);`<br>`    // auto-creates Timer + Counter + Span in Zipkin`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |

