### 🔷 Category 13: Advanced JPA / Hibernate-Specific

| # | Annotation | Framework / Module | Core Purpose & When to Use | Code Example |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 140 | `@MappedSuperclass` | JPA | Designates a class as a **base entity** whose mappings apply to subclass entities but which is not itself mapped to a table. Ideal for common auditing fields (`id`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`) shared across all entities. | `@MappedSuperclass`<br>`@EntityListeners(AuditingEntityListener.class)`<br>`@Data`<br>`public abstract class BaseEntity {`<br>`  @Id @GeneratedValue(strategy = IDENTITY)`<br>`  private Long id;`<br>`  @CreatedDate @Column(updatable = false)`<br>`  private Instant createdAt;`<br>`  @LastModifiedDate`<br>`  private Instant updatedAt;`<br>`  @Version private Long version;`<br>`}` |
| 141 | `@CreatedDate` / `@LastModifiedDate` | Spring Data JPA Auditing | Automatically populates **timestamp fields** on entity create/update events. Requires `@EnableJpaAuditing` and `@EntityListeners(AuditingEntityListener.class)` on the entity or its `@MappedSuperclass`. | `@Entity`<br>`@EntityListeners(AuditingEntityListener.class)`<br>`public class Order extends BaseEntity {`<br>`  @CreatedDate`<br>`  @Column(nullable = false, updatable = false)`<br>`  private Instant createdAt;`<br><br>`  @LastModifiedDate`<br>`  @Column(nullable = false)`<br>`  private Instant lastModifiedAt;`<br>`}` |
| 142 | `@CreatedBy` / `@LastModifiedBy` | Spring Data JPA Auditing | Automatically captures the **principal (user) who created or last modified** an entity. Requires an `AuditorAware<T>` bean that returns the current user from the `SecurityContext`. | `@Configuration`<br>`@EnableJpaAuditing`<br>`public class JpaAuditConfig {`<br>`  @Bean`<br>`  public AuditorAware<String> auditorProvider() {`<br>`    return () -> Optional.ofNullable(`<br>`      SecurityContextHolder.getContext().getAuthentication())`<br>`      .map(Authentication::getName);`<br>`  }`<br>`}`<br><br>`// Entity field:`<br>`@CreatedBy @Column(updatable = false)`<br>`private String createdBy;` |
| 143 | `@EnableJpaAuditing` | Spring Data JPA | **Activates JPA auditing** so that `@CreatedDate`, `@LastModifiedDate`, `@CreatedBy`, `@LastModifiedBy` annotations are processed. Place on a `@Configuration` class. Often placed on the main app class in small projects. | `@SpringBootApplication`<br>`@EnableJpaAuditing(auditorAwareRef = "auditorProvider")`<br>`public class InventoryServiceApp {`<br>`  public static void main(String[] args) {`<br>`    SpringApplication.run(InventoryServiceApp.class, args);`<br>`  }`<br>`}` |
| 144 | `@SQLDelete` | Hibernate (`org.hibernate.annotations`) | Overrides Hibernate''s **default DELETE SQL** with a custom statement. The go-to annotation for implementing **soft deletes** — marks records as deleted instead of physically removing them. Always pair with `@Where` to filter results. | `@Entity`<br>`@SQLDelete(sql = "UPDATE employees SET deleted = true,`<br>`  deleted_at = NOW() WHERE id = ?")`<br>`@Where(clause = "deleted = false")`<br>`public class Employee extends BaseEntity {`<br>`  @Column(nullable = false)`<br>`  private boolean deleted = false;`<br>`  private Instant deletedAt;`<br>`}` |
| 145 | `@Where` | Hibernate | Appends a **static SQL WHERE clause** to all queries on an entity or collection. Automatically filters soft-deleted records, multi-tenant rows, or active-flag filtering — without modifying every query or repository method. | `@Entity`<br>`@Where(clause = "status = ''ACTIVE'' AND tenant_id = :tenantId")`<br>`public class Product extends BaseEntity {`<br>`  private String status;`<br>`  private Long tenantId;`<br>`}`<br><br>// All findAll(), findById() etc. automatically`<br>// append WHERE status=''ACTIVE'' AND tenant_id=... |
| 146 | `@DynamicUpdate` | Hibernate | Generates an **UPDATE SQL with only changed columns** instead of all columns. Critical for wide tables (50+ columns) in high-throughput microservices — reduces network payload, avoids overwriting concurrent column changes, and improves optimistic locking precision. | `@Entity`<br>`@DynamicUpdate`<br>`public class UserProfile extends BaseEntity {`<br>`  private String displayName;`<br>`  private String bio;`<br>`  private String avatarUrl;`<br>`  // ... 40 more fields`<br>`  // UPDATE only sets changed columns:`<br>`  // UPDATE user_profile SET bio=? WHERE id=?`<br>`  // instead of: UPDATE user_profile SET displayName=?,bio=?,avatarUrl=?,... WHERE id=?`<br>`}` |
| 147 | `@DynamicInsert` | Hibernate | Generates an **INSERT SQL with only non-null columns**, letting the DB apply `DEFAULT` values for omitted columns. Useful when the DB has complex defaults (timestamps, sequences, computed columns) that should not be overridden by Java-side nulls. | `@Entity`<br>`@DynamicInsert`<br>`public class AuditLog extends BaseEntity {`<br>`  @Column(nullable = false)`<br>`  private String action;`<br>`  // DB default: created_at DEFAULT NOW()`<br>`  private Instant createdAt; // null in Java = DB sets it`<br>`  // INSERT INTO audit_log (action) VALUES (?)`<br>`  // DB fills created_at automatically`<br>`}` |
| 148 | `@BatchSize` | Hibernate | Controls **how many lazy-loaded entities are fetched per SQL round-trip** when Hibernate executes collection or proxy loading. Dramatically reduces N+1 queries (e.g., 1 query for 100 department IDs instead of 100 individual queries) without going fully EAGER. | `@Entity`<br>`public class Department extends BaseEntity {`<br>`  @OneToMany(mappedBy = "department",`<br>`    fetch = FetchType.LAZY)`<br>`  @BatchSize(size = 30)`<br>`  private List<Employee> employees;`<br>`}`<br>// Hibernate: SELECT * FROM employees WHERE dept_id IN (?, ?, ... 30 values)`<br>// Instead of 30 individual SELECT queries |
| 149 | `@FilterDef` / `@Filter` | Hibernate | Defines a **named, parameterized filter** (`@FilterDef`) and applies it to an entity or collection (`@Filter`). Unlike `@Where` (static), Hibernate filters are **toggled at runtime** per session — ideal for multi-tenancy, soft-delete visibility control, and data partitioning. | `@Entity`<br>`@FilterDef(name = "tenantFilter",`<br>`  parameters = @ParamDef(name = "tenantId", type = Long.class))`<br>`@Filter(name = "tenantFilter",`<br>`  condition = "tenant_id = :tenantId")`<br>`public class Invoice extends BaseEntity {`<br>`  private Long tenantId;`<br>`}`<br><br>`// Enable per-request in a Spring interceptor:`<br>`Session session = em.unwrap(Session.class);`<br>`session.enableFilter("tenantFilter")`<br>`  .setParameter("tenantId", currentTenantId);` |
| 150 | `@NaturalId` | Hibernate | Marks a **business key field** (e.g., email, ISBN, PAN, GSTIN) as a natural identifier. Hibernate can load entities by natural ID using a second-level cache lookup, bypassing a full table scan. Supports mutable natural IDs via `@NaturalId(mutable = true)`. | `@Entity`<br>`public class User extends BaseEntity {`<br>`  @NaturalId(mutable = false)`<br>`  @Column(nullable = false, unique = true)`<br>`  private String email;`<br>`}`<br><br>`// Efficient cache-aware lookup:`<br>`User user = session.byNaturalId(User.class)`<br>`  .using("email", "rishabh@tcs.com")`<br>`  .load();`<br>`// Uses L2 cache — no SELECT if cached` |

